<InstitutionalPage
  title="Corrections"
  eyebrow="Accountability"
  description="Material factual errors are corrected openly on the affected Nuvellum article."
  intro="Accuracy is not served by pretending an error never existed. When a factual correction changes what a reader should understand, the record should say so."
  note="Typographical and other immaterial fixes may be made quietly where meaning is unchanged."
>
  <h2>Material corrections</h2>
  <p>When a factual error materially affects the substance of a piece, Nuvellum corrects the article and discloses the change. The aim is a record that is both accurate and candid about what was amended.</p>
  <h2>Minor edits</h2>
  <p>Spelling, punctuation, formatting and other non-substantive errors may be corrected without a formal note where the change does not alter meaning, attribution or the substance of the reporting.</p>
  <h2>Raise a correction</h2>
  <p>If you believe a Nuvellum article contains a factual error, write to <a href="mailto:sam@nuvellum.news?subject=Correction%20request">sam@nuvellum.news</a>. Please include the article title, the passage in question and the factual basis for the requested correction.</p>
</InstitutionalPage>
